@startuml microservices-component
title Microservices architecture: services, REST and RabbitMQ

' Exercise 6. What Stage 2 builds. Synchronous REST where the caller needs an answer now
' (locking a spot, reading a pricing rule); RabbitMQ events for side effects.
' Routing keys match the messaging table in CLAUDE.md.

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor Driver
actor Admin
component "Frontend\nReact SPA" as FE

component "API gateway\nSpring Cloud Gateway" as GW

component "parking-service\nlocations, spots (State),\npricing rules, live status" as PS
component "reservation-service\nreservations, sessions (Facade),\ncost (Strategy)" as RS
component "payment-service\nsimulated payments (Factory)" as PayS
component "notification-service\nsimulated channels (Factory)" as NS

queue "RabbitMQ\ntopic exchange parking.events" as MQ

database "parking_db" as PDB
database "reservation_db" as RDB
database "payment_db" as PayDB
database "notification_db" as NDB

Driver --> FE
Admin --> FE
FE --> GW : HTTPS /api/v1, /ws

GW --> PS : /parking-locations/**, /activity\n/ws (STOMP, spot status, activity)
GW --> RS : /reservations/**\n/parking-sessions/**
GW --> PayS : /payments/**
GW --> NS : /notifications/**

RS -left-> PS : REST (sync): reserve / occupy\nspot, get pricing rule

PS --> PDB
RS --> RDB
PayS --> PayDB
NS --> NDB

RS ..> MQ : publishes\nreservation.created/cancelled/expired\nsession.started, session.completed
PayS ..> MQ : publishes\npayment.completed / payment.failed
PS ..> MQ : publishes\nspot.status-changed

MQ ..> PS : reservation.cancelled/expired,\nsession.completed → free spot;\nreservation.*, session.*, payment.*\n→ admin activity feed
MQ ..> PayS : session.completed\n→ charge
MQ ..> RS : payment.*\n→ record result
MQ ..> NS : reservation.*, session.completed,\npayment.* → notify

note bottom of MQ
  Each consumer has its own durable queue
  bound to the exchange; consumers dedupe
  on eventId. Reservation expiry: TTL queue
  + dead-letter exchange.
end note

@enduml
